ThreeTerm OCCT geometry worker — provenance, modifications, and build

Upstream
- Project: OpenCASCADE Technology (OCCT)
- URL: https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT
- Pinned tag: V7_9_2 (see crates/workers/occt/build.rs::OCCT_PINNED_TAG)
- Pinned commit: c5f20409c52bf8f658314d205a0e5d6f0be0969c (see crates/workers/occt/build.rs::OCCT_PINNED_SHA)
- License: LGPL-2.1 (with the OCCT static-linking exception)

Vendored files
- This slice does not vendor OCCT sources; it links against the system
  OCCT install (Archlinux community `opencascade` package on the CI
  container; `THREETERM_OCCT_DIR` override for any prebuilt tree). The
  Archlinux package version recorded at slice time is what the CI
  install resolves to. Vendoring is gated behind `THREETERM_OCCT_VENDOR=1`
  and not used in the default build.

ThreeTerm additions (NOT derived from upstream)
- src-cpp/worker_main.cpp — ThreeTerm-only worker binary that exchanges
  extrude / boolean-fuse envelopes over stdin/stdout JSON, builds OCCT
  solids (extrude via `BRepBuilderAPI_MakePolygon` + `BRepPrimAPI_MakePrism`,
  Boolean fuse via `BRepAlgoAPI_Fuse`), validates the result with
  `BRepCheck_Analyzer`, and writes the BREP to the host-staged output
  path. The worker exits 2 on a malformed request, 3 on a BREP that
  fails `BRepCheck_Analyzer`, and 0 on success.
- build.rs — ThreeTerm-only cargo build glue that locates the system
  OCCT install (`THREETERM_OCCT_DIR` / `/usr/include/opencascade` /
  `/usr/local/include/opencascade`), compiles worker_main.cpp against
  the OCCT system libraries, and writes the worker binary to
  `OUT_DIR/bin/threeterm-occt-worker`. The Rust boundary in
  `crates/workers/occt/src/lib.rs` spawns the binary as a disposable
  subprocess per request.

Build
- Prerequisites: g++ (or any C++17 compiler), the system OCCT 7.x
  development package (Archlinux: `pacman -Syu opencascade`).
- `cargo build -p threeterm-occt-worker` runs build.rs which:
    1. searches for the system OCCT install (env var first, then the
       default include / lib search paths);
    2. compiles worker_main.cpp against the OCCT system libraries
       (`TKernel`, `TKMath`, `TKG2d`, `TKG3d`, `TKGeomBase`,
       `TKGeomAlgo`, `TKBRep`, `TKTopAlgo`, `TKPrim`, `TKBO`,
        `TKFillet`, `TKShHealing`, `TKMesh`, `TKDESTL`, `TKDESTEP`,
        `TKXSBase`) and writes
       the worker binary to `OUT_DIR/bin/threeterm-occt-worker`.
- `THREETERM_OCCT_DIR=<dir>` overrides the search path.
- `THREETERM_OCCT_VENDOR=1` enables a multi-hour vendored build from
  the pinned tag (off by default; not used in CI).
- `THREETERM_SKIP_OCCTBUILD=1` skips the C++ build (test harnesses
  set this when they provide their own worker binary).
- `THREETERM_OCCTBUILD_WORKER=<path>` overrides the resolved worker
  binary path used by `OcctWorker::locate`.

Distribution obligations (LGPL-2.1)
- The worker binary dynamically links against the system OCCT shared
  libraries. Users must be able to relink the worker against a
  different OCCT version; the dynamic link contract satisfies this
  without further obligations beyond the LGPL notice and a path to
  the corresponding OCCT source (the upstream URL above).
- The worker binary embeds the pinned OCCT tag and commit SHA in
  `worker-metadata.txt` so the corresponding source for any given
  build is unambiguous.

Schema
- worker_main.cpp exchanges envelopes at schema_version
  "threeterm.workers.occt/1". The host (ThreeTerm) is the sole owner
  of stable feature_ids; OCCT numeric handles are private to the
  worker.
